for decades the rich have used offshore  havens to hide away their money and more  and more investigative journalists have  tried to expose their methods but never  before on this scale  it really kind of pulls back the veil of  secrecy that hangs over this offshore  world  it kind of reveals this global industry  of not just corporate service providers  but bankers lawyers and accountants who  are working quite hard to hide assets  to bend the rules in some cases to break  the rules for those who are wealthy or  powerful enough to pay for it  nearly 12 million confidential files  were leaked to investigators uncovering  the hidden assets of 35 current and  former world leaders more than 300  politicians and public officials  the documents come from 14 offshore  financial service providers based all  around the world  one leader singled out in what  investigators have called the pandora  papers is czech prime minister andrej  babis investigators claim he used  offshore companies to buy a 12 million  dollar chateau in the french riviera  with two swimming pools and a cinema  he has rejected the claims on twitter i  have never done anything illegal or  wrong he said but that doesn't prevent  them from trying to denigrate me again  and influence the czech parliamentary  elections  many other members of the rich the  famous the powerful are singled out in  the papers for using the offshore  financial system to hide their money and  avoid paying tax  and one location comes up more than  others despite all the controversy about  london being used to conceal huge  amounts of money the city remains the  destination of choice for many it seems  desperate to park their cash without too  many questions being asked  dominic waghorn sky news
 

